Dear Ms. Chen,

Congratulations! You have been selected for the Singapore
Airlines Cadet Pilot Programme (Class 187) beginning March 2027.

Your Application:
  Application ID: SIA-CP-2027-8842
  Programme: Cadet Pilot Programme (Class 187)
  Training: Singapore Flying College (18 months)
  Salary: SGD $5,200/month during training
  Interview: October 15, 2026 (passed)

Next Steps:

  All admission documentation is handled through the official
  SIA Careers portal:

  1. Navigate to singaporeair.com/careers in your browser
     (Type the URL manually. Do NOT click links from emails.)

  2. Go to "Application Status" → SIA-CP-2027-8842

  3. Download the Document Checklist (PDF)

  4. Submit documents by registered mail to:
     Cadet Programme Office
     Airline House, 25 Airline Road, Singapore 819829

  Required documents (certified copies):
  - Passport (all pages)
  - Birth certificate (English translation)
  - Educational certificates
  - CAAS Class 1 Medical examination report
  - Eye test report (visual acuity, color vision)
  - Police clearance certificate

  Important Security Notes:
  Singapore Airlines will NEVER:
  - Ask applicants to upload passports or medical records
    through email portals
  - Use Singpass OAuth for cadet admission verification
  - Request offline_access or any OAuth permission
  - Offer a "Chinese admission channel" for document upload
  - Send direct verification links via email

  All cadet admission documents are submitted by registered
  mail or in person at Airline House. Identity verification
  happens at the in-person medical examination (CAAS-approved
  aeromedical centre in Singapore).

  Foreign applicants do NOT need Singpass for admission —
  Singpass is for Singapore residents only.

  If you receive an email asking you to upload passports or
  medical records through a "cadet portal," it is a phishing
  attempt targeting pilot programme applicants.

Programme Details:
  Acceptance rate: <2% (4,000+ applicants, 80 seats)
  Training: Singapore + Adelaide (Australia)
  Career: Second Officer → First Officer → Captain

